<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06M5">Example <span data-tag="06M5">9.4.9.30</span>.</a> Let $U: \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be a cocartesian fibration of simplicial sets. Corollary <a data-tag="06M4" href="/tag/06M4">9.4.9.29</a> implies that $U$ is edgewise accessible (in the sense of Definition <a data-tag="06LR" href="/tag/06LR">9.4.9.16</a>) if and only if the covariant transport representation $\operatorname{Tr}_{\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}/\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}$ takes values in the $\infty $-category $\operatorname{\mathcal{QC}}^{\operatorname{Acc}}$ whose objects are accessible $\infty $-categories and whose morphisms are accessible functors (Notation <a data-tag="06L5" href="/tag/06L5">9.4.8.11</a>). Similarly, Corollary <a data-tag="06M2" href="/tag/06M2">9.4.9.27</a> guarantees that a cartesian fibration is edgewise accessible if and only if its contravariant transport representation takes values in $\operatorname{\mathcal{QC}}^{\operatorname{Acc}}$. </p>
